<article id="entry-agathoergeo-bdag" class="entry-card" data-dictionary="grego" hidden data-source="BDAG">
            <header class="entry-header">
                <div>
                    <h1 class="entry-title greek">ἀγαθοεργέω</h1>
                    <div class="entry-meta">
                        <span class="transliteration">⟦agathoergéō⟧</span>
                        <span class="separator">·</span>
                        <span>verbo</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="source-tag">BDAG</div>
            </header>

            <div class="entry-divider"></div>

            <section class="entry-section">
                <div class="section-title">Tradução literal</div>

                <p class="entry-text">
                    (Pitágoras, <em>Ep.</em> 10 p. 607;
                    forma contraída
                    <span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="ἀγαθουργέω" data-meanings="fazer o bem|beneficiar">ἀγαθουργέω</span>
                    em
                    <a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.14.17" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">At 14.17</a>;
                    exceto pelo uso na literatura patrística, o verbo é bastante raro, mas
                    <span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="ἀγαθουργός" data-meanings="que faz o bem|benfeitor">ἀγαθουργός</span>
                    e
                    <span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="ἀγαθουργίη" data-meanings="beneficência|ação de fazer o bem">ἀγαθουργίη</span>
                    remontam a Heródoto
                    [<span class="biblio-ref tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="biblio" data-tooltip-label="B-D-F §119, 1" data-tooltip-text="Blass-Debrunner-Funk, §119, 1">B-D-F §119, 1</span>]).
                    <strong>Fazer aquilo que beneficia outros, fazer o bem, conferir benefícios</strong>:
                    dos ricos,
                    <a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.6.18" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">1 Tm 6.18</a>;
                    de Deus,
                    <a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.14.17" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">At 14.17</a>.
                    —
                    <span class="biblio-ref tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="biblio" data-tooltip-label="TW" data-tooltip-text="Theologisches Wörterbuch zum Neuen Testament">TW.</span>
                </p>
            </section>
        </article>

